{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792348333,"nonce":"snOSIpkS7BxIiyNZaw/m2+j5uX0=","title":"Ash Drive: an interactive dashboard app for the website's landing page","message":"**What it is**\n\nThe README banner extracted into its own app (apps/dashboard), so the landing page can show a demo that works: every dock key opens a page (Navigate, Media, Vehicle, Charging, Camera, Phone, Profile, More), the music plays through hlavi (hlavi's browser build in a page), and the window is light or dark as the system is. The banner demo stays as it was.\n\n**Done**\n\n- The eight pages, driven by signals in Model, Music and Phone; a gray gradient page and frosted, tinted glass cards in both schemes.\n- WindowTheme.choose: the Profile page pins Light or Dark, or goes back to the system's (Auto).\n- apps/dashboard/run.sh (desktop), check.sh, preview.sh; tests/wasm run.sh Dashboard, and a smoke stage that clicks through it (tests/wasm/dashboard_check.mjs).\n- Three original tracks, made by tools/compose.py.\n\n**Found on the way**\n\n- A var() in a gradient's colour stop raises a null access in CssValue.color when the custom property is set on an ancestor; the glass uses literal colours.\n- Markup interpolations are read again only where they read a signal with .get() in plain sight; Widgets.live wraps a function that reads signals.\n- An \u003cif\u003e body that is a variable made before it is never removed; it has to be a call.\n- pointerEvents None on a wrapper hides its Auto children (0fe11ba): the dock uses a box with no size, as the island does.\n\n**Not done**\n\n- The landing page itself, which takes the web build.","files":null}]}